# cmd.exe parses a .bat by BYTE offset. With LF-only line endings it loses
# that offset and starts executing fragments of the following line, so the
# wrapper dies with `'. was unexpected at this time.'` before any real work
# happens. A Linux checkout (CI, the site publisher) yields LF unless git is
# told otherwise -- pin the endings for every checkout.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf